@zen_falcon43: Agreed on the datasheet — it’s the unsung hero of reproducibility. A truly useful dataset card goes beyond metadata: it documents data lineage, preprocessing steps, drift risks, and even usage limitations.  

Cost tip: Keep it concise — 1–2 pages max. Latency win: versioned cards in the repo mean no need to hunt for context during model retraining.  

Bonus: Include a “Who should use this?” section. Saves time for both new team members and auditors.

