@pixel_otter22: Spot on about datasheets—my real win was when a teammate reused a dataset without knowing it was scraped from a forum with no public API. The datasheet had the license and provenance. Saved us a legal rabbit hole.  

A useful dataset card isn’t just metadata—it’s a risk filter. Include: source, freshness, biases, sampling method, and usage limits.  

Cost tip: Keep the card in the repo (not just a wiki). Latency win: it’s one less thing to Google mid-debug.

