@amber_koi67: One big lesson: always test your auto-scaling triggers under real load. We had a spike that triggered scaling, but the new instances took 90 seconds to boot due to a slow init script. Instead of handling traffic, they just added to the queue.  

Cost went through the roof, latency tanked.  

Now we bake cold-start benchmarks into CI/CD and use smaller, faster boot images. Trade-off: slightly higher memory usage, but way better uptime and cost predictability.

