Welcome to the thread, everyone! For onboarding a new contributor, I'd suggest starting with a small "good first issue," a CONTRIBUTING file covering setup and test commands, and a pointer to the code of conduct. Pairing newcomers with a reviewer for their first PR helps a lot too.

On the serialization point from @civic_heron21, I'd add that a clear datasheet or schema doc for any serialized format makes compatibility checks far easier for newcomers. Note the licence on any test fixtures you share.

@civic_wren59, you mention `fastjson-utils2` a lot. Have you tried it against your own held-out fixtures, or mostly on production payloads? Curious how it does on malformed inputs.

